---
description: Labels, accessible names, instructions, errors, required fields, and autocomplete for forms
alwaysApply: false
globs:
  - "**/*.{html,htm,js,jsx,ts,tsx,vue,svelte,mdx}"
---

Lexable forms-and-inputs:

- Every input, select, and textarea needs a visible label that is programmatically associated (for/id or wrapping label). Placeholder is not a label (3.3.2, 4.1.2, 1.3.1).
- Required fields must be indicated in text, not by color alone. aria-required or required can supplement, not replace, the visible indication.
- Error messages must identify the field in text and, where possible, be tied with aria-describedby or aria-errormessage (3.3.1). aria-invalid is not a complete error message.
- Instructions needed to complete a field must be available before submission.
- For personal data fields (name, email, username, password, organization, street, city, country, postal code, phone, credit-card fields), set autocomplete to the appropriate token (1.3.5) when the field collects that data.
- Do not disable paste on password or one-time-code fields. Accessible authentication is not fully testable statically; mark related flows needs manual review.
- Group related radios and checkboxes with fieldset and legend.
